exam: It is given that the number of {t} held by {a} is {k} times the number held by {b}, and that the aggregate held by both is {s}. Determine the number of {t} held by {a}.
exam: Ascertain the quantity of {t} in the possession of {a}, whereas {a} and {b} together possess {s} {t} and the holding of {a} is {k} times that of {b}.
exam: Two quantities, the first being {k} times the second, have a sum of {s}. State the value of the first quantity.
exam: Whereas a total of {s} {t} is divided between {a} and {b} in such a manner that the share of {a} is {k} times the share of {b}, compute the share of {a}.
exercise: When Grandad passed away, he left {s} stamps to {a} and {b}, and {a}, the eldest, got {k} times as many as {b}. How many stamps did {a} get?
exercise: {a}'s dad was let go, so {a} and {b} put {s} dollars of their savings towards the rent. {a} gives {k} times as much as {b}. How many dollars does {a} give?
